<title>GERMANY: German 9-mth major media revs up six pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German 9-mth major media revs up six pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gross advertising revenues for the major media segments rose six percent in the first nine months of 1996 from the same period a year ago, the IPA Plus media agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>The agency, publishing data provided by Dun and Bradstreet's Nielsen research unit, gave the following details in its latest report covering advertising revenue from January to September.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of marks unless stated.)</p>
<p>			   AD REVS	  AD REVS	 MKT  SHR</p>
<p>			   Jan-Sept 96   Jan-Sept 95     Sept 96</p>
<p>PRINT MEDIA</p>
<p> Newspapers	     4,106	   4,007	    22.4 pct</p>
<p> General magazines    4,398	   4,364	    23.9 pct</p>
<p> Trade magazines	  597	     611	     3.2 pct</p>
<p> Billboards		 592	     534	     3.2 pct</p>
<p>ELECTRONIC MEDIA</p>
<p> Television	     7,523	   6,624	    41.0 pct</p>
<p> Radio		    1,150	   1,175	     6.3 pct</p>
<p> TOTAL REVENUE	 18,366	  17,318</p>
<p>NOTE - The data do not include direct mail, listings magazines, or newspaper supplements.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 2609750</p>
</text>
